.DS_Store
.git/
.gitignore
*.swp
*.bak
*.tmp
*.orig
*~
# A site values file, if anybody leaves a copy in here: it names a node, a host path and
# a hostname, and this repository is public. README.md says to keep it in
# `kube-cluster-helm-values` instead. `values-example.yaml`, which names nothing real, is
# deliberately outside this pattern so that it ships with the chart.
#
# There is no `!`-negated exemption anywhere in this file, because Helm's .helmignore is
# NOT gitignore: `pkg/ignore` has no negation, and a line beginning with `!` breaks the
# rest of the file silently -- `helm show chart` then reports "Chart.yaml file is
# missing", which is a confusing way to be told about a typo in an ignore rule.
values-site*.yaml
